{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Adjust colors, levels, black point, and white point"], "extent": [12, 68]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Color correction nodes in compositing networks appear with a blue\nbackground. Houdini collapses consecutive color correction nodes into\none operation, saving memory, improving performance and avoiding\nclipping/quantization issues."], "extent": [112, 345]}, {"type": "tip_group", "body": [{"type": "tip", "indent": 0, "role": "item", "extent": [345, 350], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The Bright, Contrast, and Gamma operations can optionally affect\n    individual channels."], "extent": [350, 445]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"tag": "table", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 0, "extent": [445, 453], "body": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [453, 462], "body": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" To adjust\u2026"], "extent": [462, 488]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Use this operator"], "extent": [488, 519]}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [519, 528], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Brightness"], "extent": [528, 552]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [552, 565], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/bright", "type": "link", "text": ["Bright COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/bright.html"}], "extent": [565, 607]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [607, 616], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Contrast"], "extent": [616, 638]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [638, 651], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/contrast", "type": "link", "text": ["Contrast COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/contrast.html"}], "extent": [651, 697]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [697, 706], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Gamma"], "extent": [706, 725]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [725, 738], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/gamma", "type": "link", "text": ["Gamma COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/gamma.html"}], "extent": [738, 778]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [778, 787], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Brightness, Contrast, and Gamma for the overall image,"], "extent": [787, 855]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["highlights, midtones, and lowlights\n        td>>"], "extent": [855, 912], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/colorcorrect", "type": "link", "text": ["Color Correct COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/colorcorrect.html"}], "extent": [912, 967]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [967, 976], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Map one color range to another"], "extent": [976, 1020]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [1020, 1033], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/colormap", "type": "link", "text": ["Color Map COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/colormap.html"}], "extent": [1033, 1080]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [1080, 1089], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Clamp minimum and/or maximum color values"], "extent": [1089, 1144]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [1144, 1157], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/limit", "type": "link", "text": ["Limit COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/limit.html"}], "extent": [1157, 1197]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [1197, 1206], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Hue, saturation, and/or value"], "extent": [1206, 1249]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [1249, 1262], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/hsv", "type": "link", "text": ["HSV COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/hsv.html"}], "extent": [1262, 1298]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [1298, 1307], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Color curves"], "extent": [1307, 1333]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [1333, 1346], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/colorcurve", "type": "link", "text": ["Color Curve COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/colorcurve.html"}, " or ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/huecurve", "type": "link", "text": ["Hue Curve\n            COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/huecurve.html"}], "extent": [1346, 1447]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"level": 2, "id": "comp_blackwhite", "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Black point and white point"], "extent": [1447, 1499], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["For planes with integer data, by default 0 means black and the\n    maximum value (which depends on whether you are using 8, 16, or\n    32-bit integers) is white. However, you can adjust which level\n    corresponds to black and which level corresponds to white. This\n    allows you to reduce the head and foot clipping errors at the\n    expense of quantization errors."], "extent": [1499, 1873]}, {"type": "note_group", "body": [{"type": "note", "indent": 4, "role": "item", "extent": [1873, 1883], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["For planes with floating point data, 0 is ", {"type": "em", "text": ["always"]}, " black and the\n        maximum value is ", {"type": "em", "text": ["always"]}, " white. You cannot set black and white\n        points for floating point data."], "extent": [1883, 2069]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["For example, a 16 bit image with black and white points set at\n    24,000 and 40,000 gives you 16,000 levels between black and white,\n    and quite a bit of head and foot room (the full range is -1.5 to\n    2.6)."], "extent": [2069, 2287]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Houdini always displays color values as a range from 0 to 1. So, if\n    you adjust the black/white points, you can have values less than 0\n    or greater than 1, which reduces clipping of values during\n    calculations."], "extent": [2287, 2512]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["For example, for an 8-bit integer channel, you could set the black\n    point to 64 and the white point to 192. In Houdini, the 0 color\n    value now corresponds to a value of 64 in the channel, and the 1\n    color value now corresponds to a value of 192 in the channel. So,\n    the range of color values you can use in Houdini is now from\n    (0-64)/(192-64) = -0.5 to (255-64)/(192-64) = 1.492."], "extent": [2512, 2913]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["To set the black point and white point of an image, use the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/levels", "type": "link", "text": ["Levels\n    operator"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/levels.html"}, "."], "extent": [2913, 3019]}]}], "title": ["Adjust colors, levels, black point, and white point"], "included": ["/composite/_old_cops_deprecated"]}